---
import FullAnalysis from "../components/FullAnalysis.astro";
import PageShell from "../layouts/PageShell.astro";
import CustomerFunnel from "../components/CustomerFunnel.astro";
import RideFunnel from "../components/RideFunnel.astro";
import SchoolComparison from "../components/SchoolComparison.astro";
import { customerFunnel } from "../data/funnels.js";

const requesters = customerFunnel.stages[2];
const completers = customerFunnel.stages[3];
---

<PageShell
  title="Metrocar — Where Do We Lose Momentum?"
  description="A Master School funnel analysis project: where Metrocar loses customers, what the recorded evidence shows, and what it cannot explain."
>
  <main id="main-content" class="overview-main metrocar-project" tabindex="-1">
    <section id="introduction" class="project-introduction project-width" aria-labelledby="project-title" tabindex="-1">
      <div class="project-intro-panel">
        <header class="project-section-header">
          <p class="eyebrow"><a class="masterschool-link" href="https://joinmsit.de/vergleich/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Master School Project <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a> · Ride-sharing funnel analysis</p>
          <h1 id="project-title">Metrocar — Where Do We Lose Momentum?</h1>
        </header>
        <div class="project-intro-copy">
          <p>Metrocar connects riders and drivers. The project examines separate customer and ride funnels.</p>
          <p class="project-intro-lead"><strong>🎯 Goal:</strong> Find the weakest customer-funnel transition and test what ride records can—and cannot—explain.</p>
          <nav class="project-sections" aria-label="Project sections">
            <a href="#school-to-rebuild">School → rebuild</a>
            <a href="#question">Question</a>
            <a href="#dashboard">Business Dashboard</a>
            <a href="#full-analysis">Full Analysis</a>
            <a href="#what-we-learned">Wrap-up</a>
          </nav>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <SchoolComparison />

    <section id="question" class="project-question project-width" aria-labelledby="project-question-title" tabindex="-1">
      <p class="eyebrow">The question</p>
      <h2 id="project-question-title">Where does Metrocar lose customers on the path from app download to a completed ride?</h2>
      <p>Which transition has the weakest conversion, and what can recorded ride history tell us about it?</p>
    </section>

    <section id="dashboard" class="metrocar-dashboard project-width" aria-labelledby="dashboard-title" tabindex="-1">
      <header class="project-section-header dashboard-hero">
        <h2 id="dashboard-title">Business Dashboard</h2>
        <p>Recorded funnels at two distinct grains: customer progression and individual rides.</p>
      </header>

      <section class="finding-panel" aria-labelledby="finding-title">
        <h3 id="finding-title"><strong>{completers.percentOfPrevious}</strong><span>of requesters completed<br class="desktop-break" /> at least one ride.</span></h3>
        <p><span class="finding-scope">Overall · all platforms and ages</span><strong>{completers.count.toLocaleString("en-US")} of {requesters.count.toLocaleString("en-US")}</strong> requesting users<br />Requested ≥1 → Completed ≥1</p>
      </section>

      <div class="funnel-grid" aria-label="Metrocar funnel visualizations">
        <article class="funnel-panel funnel-panel--customer" aria-labelledby="customer-panel-title">
          <header class="panel-header">
            <div><p class="panel-kicker">Primary customer evidence</p><h3 id="customer-panel-title">Customer Funnel</h3></div>
            <span class="grain-pill">Entrant / user stage</span>
          </header>
          <CustomerFunnel />
        </article>
        <article class="funnel-panel funnel-panel--ride" aria-labelledby="ride-panel-title">
          <header class="panel-header">
            <div><p class="panel-kicker">Supporting ride path</p><h3 id="ride-panel-title">Ride Funnel</h3></div>
            <span class="grain-pill">One <code>ride_id</code></span>
          </header>
          <RideFunnel />
          <p class="panel-note">Reviewed means reviewed rides inside the Approved-payment path.</p>
        </article>
      </div>

      <section class="overview-close" aria-labelledby="takeaway-title">
        <div>
          <h3 id="takeaway-title">The loss is clear. Its cause is not.</h3>
          <p>Acceptance elsewhere in a user's ride history does not establish the cause of non-completion.</p>
        </div>
        <a class="primary-button" href="#full-analysis">Explore Full Analysis <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
      </section>
      <p class="dashboard-next-step"><strong>Next step:</strong> investigate same-ride operational or cancellation evidence.</p>
      <ul class="trust-strip" aria-label="Project methods and validation">
        <li>Python · pandas · SQL · Plotly</li>
        <li>Customer grain + <code>ride_id</code> grain</li>
        <li>SQL ↔ pandas reconciled — Q01–Q10 only</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <FullAnalysis />

    <section id="what-we-learned" class="project-learning project-width" aria-labelledby="learning-title" tabindex="-1">
      <div class="learning-panel">
        <header class="project-section-header learning-header">
          <p class="eyebrow">Return to the question</p>
          <h2 id="learning-title">Wrap-up</h2>
          <p>The funnel revealed the weakest step. Ride histories helped test an explanation.</p>
        </header>
        <ol class="learning-takeaways" role="list" aria-label="From recorded journeys to the question we carry forward">
          <li>
            <h3><span class="learning-number" aria-hidden="true">01</span>Data — What did we use?</h3>
            <p>Recorded downloads, signups, ride events, payments and reviews let us trace customer progress separately from individual rides.</p>
            <a href="#understand-the-app-downloads-table-grain">Source and grain ↑</a>
          </li>
          <li>
            <h3><span class="learning-number" aria-hidden="true">02</span>Information — What did we find?</h3>
            <p>The largest relative customer loss was from requesting to completing a ride. Yet most non-completing requesters had a recorded acceptance somewhere in their ride history.</p>
            <a href="#diagnostic-1-did-non-completing-requesters-ever-have-an-accepted-ride">Acceptance-history evidence ↑</a>
          </li>
          <li>
            <h3><span class="learning-number" aria-hidden="true">03</span>Knowledge — What is the insight?</h3>
            <p>This challenges “never received an acceptance” as an explanation for most non-completing users.</p>
            <aside class="learning-insight" aria-label="Key insight">
              <strong>Insight</strong>
              <p>An acceptance somewhere in a user’s history does not establish why a particular ride remained unfinished.</p>
            </aside>
            <a href="#learning-slice-4-which-adjacent-transition-is-weakest">Weakest transition ↑</a>
          </li>
          <li>
            <h3><span class="learning-number" aria-hidden="true">04</span>Wisdom — What is the next question?</h3>
            <p>Link each unfinished ride’s request, any recorded acceptance and outcome. Examine operational or cancellation evidence before proposing changes.</p>
            <p class="carry-forward-question"><span>The question we carry forward</span>Which same-ride evidence would help investigate why requesting users did not complete a ride?</p>
            <a href="#visualization-2-how-many-rides-followed-the-strict-ride-path">Definitions and evidence limits ↑</a>
          </li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</PageShell>
